    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22217" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-assŭētus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unaccustomed</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 450</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					A. 1, 300</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">at vestigia nuda sinusque Cingere, inassuetum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>unusual</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 236</span></i>
			: opere inassueto Galliis, Fragm. Or. Claud. ap. Grut. 502, 2,
			37.</div>
